			<div class="content" id="post-content-1583231">
									

<p>An interesting, weird idea that's well-written and executed. I'm giving this an upvote, but I have a few nitpicks:</p>
<ul>
<li>I don't like that the last numeral of the year that this was recovered was redacted. There's no reason for it.</li>
<li><em>Die Hard</em> came out in 1988, not 1974.</li>
<li>I don't get the note. Who's Carter? It sounds like Derwent Masterson is sending the SCP as a gift to someone named Carter, but it's recovered among Derwent's effects.</li>
<li>Also, I don't particularly care for the &quot;dude commits suicide&quot; angle here. It's either implying that the SCP made him lose his mind or something, which feels a bit much, or it's an extraneous red herring.</li>
</ul>

